    "created_at": "2026-05-27T18:37:44Z",
    "updated_at": "2026-05-27T18:37:44Z",
    "body": "The Chromium implementation currently requires VID, PID and serial number to match to recognize a device when it reconnects. Devices without serial numbers do not get persistent permissions. It is possible that the bus path could be used as well but this is currently unimplemented. The specification itself leaves these details up to implementations.\n\nIf it is not possible to add a serial number to the device firmware then a workaround, since it sounds like you are operating in some kind of managed environment, is to use the [WebUsbAllowDevicesForUrls](https://chromeenterprise.google/policies/#WebUsbAllowDevicesForUrls) enterprise policy to automatically grant the site access to the device by VID and PID so the device will always appear in `getDevices()` when connected.",
    "author_association": "COLLABORATOR",
    "pin": null,
