    "created_at": "2026-07-17T17:19:35Z",
    "updated_at": "2026-07-17T17:19:35Z",
    "body": "@reillyeon I have a follow up question.  I was actually able to get the hardware manufacturer for the device update the firmware for us so it now sends the serial number with the USB device descriptor.  I have also confirmed on Chromium browsers on Mac OS, this solves the problem since the \"connected\" events now fire on a disconnect => reconnect and getDevices( ) returns previously approved devices.\n\nHowever, in Chromium on Android, it seems either the Android OS or the specific Chromium build for Android is redacting the serial number.\n\nI can see this on both platforms going to the url `chrome://device-log` and plugging a device in, unplugging, etc.\n\nSame device, same firmware, different OS, Android Chromium serial number shows up empty.\n\nDo you know if this redaction is in Chromium itself or Android, and where I can go to open a ticket to lobby for unblocking this.\n\nI am still working on trying to get the Chromium Enterprise Policy Manager in place as an alternative solution.",
