    "body": "@reillyeon i finally got it to work with chrome enterprise policy!  this is actually super beneficial for a lot of other reasons because now i can control all the policies.\n\n...and it works!  With one caveat.  If i power cycle the device off/on or unplug/plugin it does fire the `connected` event, and our software calls `getDevices` and it is returned, and I believe it makes a request to `connect` -- when this happens it does pop up a user prompt like this:\n\n`Allow Chrome to access (name of device)?   [CANCEL] [OK]` \n\nSo, even though the user does not have to see a list of devices in a pop-up modal that match the product/vendor id and select one...that part of it is skipped, but they still have to approve the final cancel / ok.\n\nI'm assuming there is no other way to configure this prompt to go away and not be necessary?",
